  "description": "Compile-time twin of six of Thessera's startup checks: an aggregate without [AggregateName], a domain event without [EventName], an aggregate whose parameterless constructor is not private, a child entity whose constructor is not internal, and an aggregate- or entity-state that names the wrong type as itself are now a build error instead of a message the first affected host prints at boot, or an InvalidCastException on the first applied event. Ships no Thessera runtime code - reference it from every host, regardless of which store it selects.",
